                <pb facs="0406" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/6428: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-10T17:00:00+01:00">September 10, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>407. My 404, September 8, 1 p.m. A high official of the Foreign Office told me
                    today that Italy has no intention of replying to the second Soviet note and that
                    consideration might eventually have to be given to severance of diplomatic
                    relations with that country.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
